<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!--
        A few example invites, built in Python rather than written out here.

        An invite needs two real partners and this module ships none, so an
        XML `ref` would tie it to whichever demo data happened to be
        installed. The method picks whatever customers exist and does nothing
        at all once a single invite is on file - so a shop that has started
        referring people never sprouts examples.

        Not noupdate, for the reason mart369_cart's deal demo gives: with it,
        the function would only ever run on a fresh install, and a shop
        upgrading into this feature would never see the examples. The method
        guards itself instead, so running on every upgrade seeds exactly once.
    -->
    <data>
        <function model="mart369.referral" name="_mart369_load_demo"/>
    </data>
</odoo>
